nL(f,P)={m}_{11}+{m}_{21}+{m}_{12}+{m}_{22}.\n$$\n\nNow, notice that\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y-1$ increases as $x$ increases, and\n\n- $f(x,y)=x+y-1$ increases as $y$ increases.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/b3c2a3891860a8ad88d2f111a3e279a65398a37020ab2f0843f8475dfd38df15.png)\n\nAs a result, the *minimum* value of $f$ in each subregion is attained when we have the *smallest* possible $x$ and the *smallest* possible $y.$ This is the value at the *bottom left corner* of each subregion.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14072149/assets/76cbbcf7ddff625cf035d6f7e37acbc6d278734cc87648ef6a88f8ace61f731e.png)\n\nHence:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{m}_{11} & =f(1,0)=0 \\\\ {m}_{21} & =f(2,0)=1 \\\\ {m}_{12} & =f(1,1)=1 \\\\ {m}_{22} & =f(2,1)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L(f,P) & =0+1+1+2 \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535925 true] [17592186374766 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374767 13194139535925 true] [17592186374766 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374768 13194139535925 true] [17592186374766 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374769 13194139535925 true] [17592186374766 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374770 13194139535925 true] [17592186374766 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374771 13194139535925 true] [17592186374766 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535925 true] [17592186374766 1041 "selection" 13194139535925 true] [17592186374766 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374770 13194139535925 true] [17592186374766 1110 #uuid "afd4c7e4-7e14-5574-80f0-31b37c14cae3" 13194139535925 true] [17592186374767 1034 "3" 13194139535925 true] [17592186374767 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535925 true] [17592186374767 1111 #uuid "fe2372d2-8d7d-51c5-8c84-006d0dafc353" 13194139535925 true] [17592186374768 1034 "2" 13194139535925 true] [17592186374768 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535925 true] [17592186374768 1111 #uuid "c383c7f1-177e-5435-a49a-cf39f18edcfe" 1319